meta {
  name: 06 Lab Report - Print (real report)
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/{{labReportId}}/print
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "type": "lab_report",
    "templateId": "{{labReportTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Production path: renders lab report `{{labReportId}}` (single test) with the
  `lab_report` template. `type` only chooses the fallback template when
  `templateId` is omitted; the same report record renders either way.

  Requires a real `{{labReportId}}`. Seed one via the Technician Reporting flow.

  `{test_file_attachment}` in the template prints the PDF(s) uploaded for THIS
  report with the Test Entry "File +" button (`LabReportAttachment.kind =
  'file'`), drawn in place page by page. To try it, attach one first with
  `16 Create Report Attachment` (`kind: "file"`, a `.pdf` `fileUrl`).

  Tag notes:
  - `{patient_age}` — one unit from the DOB as of today (tenant timezone):
    0-29 days → `N Days`, under 1 year → `N Months`, else `N Years`. Falls
    back to the stored age/age type when the patient has no DOB.
  - `{order_date}` / `{order_date_time}` — the operator-entered order time
    when one was typed (with the order date), else the order's `createdAt`
    in the tenant timezone (e.g. `01/10/2026 2:24 PM`). A back/advance-dated
    order with no typed time prints its date only.
  - `{order_id_barcode}` — Code 128 barcode IMAGE of the Order ID
    (`Order.orderCode`, e.g. `ORD-00113`).
  - `{order_id_qr_code}` — Code 128 barcode IMAGE of the Sample ID (this
    report's `OrderSample.barcode`; a barcode despite the tag name).
  - Both barcode tags render the same image whether written `{tag}`,
    `{{image:tag}}` or `<img src="{tag}" alt="…">` (the value is a
    `data:image/png;base64,…` URI rendered from the ID).

  ## Notes sections left out of the print

  The five Notes tags (`{useful_for}`, `{interpretation}`, `{limitations}`,
  `{remarks}`, `{references}`) are blank for any section the technician left out
  of THIS report (`PATCH /lab-reports/:id/note-print-sections`). It applies only
  while the matching Branch Setting (Branch Admin > Branch Settings > Technician Settings > Report Printing) is on (Lab Panel switch for a report on a
  panel order line, Lab Test switch otherwise, read from the branch that holds the
  report); while it is off every section prints. A flat template hides the heading
  and box of a blank section by wrapping the block in `{{#if useful_for}}...{{/if}}`
  (see docs/PRINT-TEMPLATES.md); a Latte template uses `{if $test->useful_for}`.

  ## Lab panel tags

  `{is_lab_panel}` is `Yes` when the test being printed belongs to a lab panel (its
  order line was ordered as a panel: each member test of a panel, and an old
  combined panel report) and empty otherwise; `{lab_panel_name}` and
  `{lab_panel_code}` give the panel. Use `{{#if is_lab_panel}}...{{/if}}` in the
  header, body or footer to show a block only for panel tests. A Latte template
  uses `{if $test->is_lab_panel}...{else}...{/if}` (a real boolean). Nothing is
  stored: the tags are read from the report's order line when it is printed.
}
